# Player scale lock (shipped, do not regress)

Anthony signed off on this layout on 2026-09-04: the course player stays visible and **scale-to-fits 16:9/4:3 on any monitor (HDMI included)** without bouncing, shrinking away, or going blank.

**Do not** edit scale/layout in [`src/hooks/useScaleToFit.ts`](src/hooks/useScaleToFit.ts) or the preview stage in [`src/App.tsx`](src/App.tsx) (`measureScaleToFit`, `useScaleTransform`, `scaler.outerStyle` / `frameStyle`, the empty measure overlay, the in-flow centering host) unless the user **explicitly** asks to change player scaling.

Image extract, QC, TTS, generate-speed, and other work must not retune player size.

## Required structure

- Measure an **empty** `absolute inset-0` overlay (not the player).
- Keep a **full-size in-flow** centering host (`flex-1` / `w-full h-full`) so the stage cannot collapse to a blank screen.
- Scale the 1280×720 (or 4:3) frame with `transform: scale` from top-left; no CSS transition on width/height/transform.
- Phones and desktop 16:9/4:3 both use this. `'full'` skips it. Desktop “Mobile” bezel is separate chrome.
- Never toggle flex-fill vs transform from measured `scale`. Never multiply scale by 0.99 against a child-sized host.

## Known failure modes (do not reintroduce)

- Flex-fill only on desktop → HDMI shows a small frame and empty space.
- Measuring the scaled player / shrink-wrapping parent → canvas animates to nothing.
- `absolute inset-0` as the only player host (no in-flow filler) → blank white stage, TOC still visible.
- CSS `cqw`/`cqh` letterbox instead of JS scale-to-fit → HDMI scale-up gone.
- `transition-all` on the frame → diagonal bounce loop.
